WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:11.440
This March, fifteen international students formed a Gen Z APEC Reporters team and visited the 2026 Greater Bay Area Flower Show in Shenzhen.
今年3月，15名国际学生组成了一支Z世代APEC记者团，参观了在深圳举办的2026粤港澳大湾区花展。

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.540
The event was the first youth communication activity of the APEC “China Year” in Shenzhen.
这次活动是APEC“中国年”在深圳的第一场青年交流活动。

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.950
The students walked through creatively designed gardens.
学生们穿行在一座座设计富有创意的展园中。

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.550
They took photos and shared stories about green development from a global perspective.
他们拍了照片，还从全球视角分享了关于绿色发展的故事。

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.600
The event aimed to show Shenzhen as a “city of parks” and spread green ideas.
这次活动旨在展现深圳这座“公园之城”的风貌，并传播绿色理念。

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.210
A French student loved the flowers.
一名法国学生很喜欢那些花。

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.080
Two Russian students admired the iris, which is this year’s theme flower.
两名俄罗斯学生很欣赏今年的主题花——鸢尾花。

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.890
One of them praised the Dapeng garden for its bright colors.
其中一人称赞大鹏展园色彩鲜艳。

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:49.320
A student from Turkmenistan was deeply moved by the Nanshan garden, calling it shiny and bright.
一名来自土库曼斯坦的学生被南山展园深深打动，称它闪闪发光、明亮耀眼。

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.540
A Nigerian student said that being in nature brings peace and relaxation.
一名尼日利亚学生说，身处大自然能带来平静与放松。

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:00.250
Besides enjoying the views, the students also documented their visit in many ways.
除了欣赏风景，学生们还用多种方式记录了这次参观。

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:08.480
One Russian student wrote a blog post highlighting the City Garden of Shenzhen, while another made short videos for online sharing.
一名俄罗斯学生写了一篇博客文章，重点介绍深圳城市园；另一名则制作了短视频，用来在网上分享。

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:18.240
The visitors said they would continue to document Shenzhen’s green development through videos and posts, presenting an eco-friendly and open city to the world.
这些参观者表示，将继续通过视频和帖子记录深圳的绿色发展，向世界展现一座环保、开放的城市。

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.970
“Gardens are small, but they carry big ideas of green development,” one member said.
“展园虽小，却承载着绿色发展的大理念。”一名成员说。

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:30.950
“We are honored to tell Shenzhen’s stories and strengthen communication between the Greater Bay Area and the world.”
“我们很荣幸能讲述深圳的故事，并加强粤港澳大湾区与世界之间的交流。”

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:47.820
The flower show ran through April 6, bringing together designers and works from APEC member economies across four sections—Master Garden, Bay Area Garden, City Garden, and Floral Market—along with eight mini-gardens, showing over 30 fantastic creations.
花展一直持续到4月6日，汇集了来自APEC成员经济体的设计师和作品，分布在大师园、湾区园、城市园和花卉市集四个展区，另有八座小型展园，展出了30多件精彩的创意作品。

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:57.870
The team will continue to visit key places of Shenzhen’s APEC-themed activities, recording the city’s development and sharing its youthful energy with the world.
这支记者团将继续走访深圳APEC主题活动的重要场所，记录这座城市的发展，并与世界分享它的青春活力。
